  "prefLabel": "Env-A 105.43 Untreated wood",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 105.43 “Untreated wood” means any timber, board, or sawn dimensional lumber that has not been treated, coated, or preserved. The term does not include any manufactured building material, such as plywood or waferboard.\n\nSource. #6283-A, eff 7-10-96; renumbered by #8256 (from Env-A 101.294), (see Revision Note #1 at chapter heading); renumbered by #8304 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading); renumbered by #9839 (from Env-A 101.208), (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading); renumbered by #10549, (from Env-A 101.210); ss by #13105, eff 9-25-20 (formerly Env-A 101.211) (see Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-A 100)",
